# A sweep produces ~7 MB, and 5 MB of that is the raw agent transcript. Every
# number taken from it already lives in the sweep's runs.jsonl (tool calls by
# name, final message, cost, tokens), so the transcript stays local for
# forensics and out of history for weight.
results/*/runs/*/stream.jsonl
results/*/runs/*/cwd/

# Per-run copies nothing reads: record.json is the same record as that run's
# line in runs.jsonl, and mcp.json is the run's MCP config, which names paths
# on the machine that ran it.
results/*/runs/*/record.json
results/*/runs/*/mcp.json

# The exported STEP files DO stay committed, deliberately: they are the one
# thing a future oracle version cannot reconstruct, and re-grading an old sweep
# with a better oracle is worth 1 MB a run. runs.jsonl cites each one
# (`facts.file`).
